        <briefdescription>
<para>Approximate equality comparator, with an explicit tolerance. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The comparison succeeds if the distance between <computeroutput>lhs</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>rhs</computeroutput> is less than or equal to <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput>, so a tolerance of zero requires equal values. The operands are numbers, integral or floating-point, possibly of different types (the deprecated value wrappers and numeric literals are also accepted, and their own tolerance is not used). For the integers, the distance is computed exactly, also for operands of different signedness, so <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx</ref> (0u, -1, 2)</computeroutput> succeeds; for the other types, in their common floating-point type. A failure is reported as <computeroutput>lhs ~ (rhs +/- epsilon)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">t.expect<sp/>(mt::approx<sp/>(read_adc<sp/>(),<sp/>512,<sp/>3))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;ADC<sp/>reading&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">t.expect<sp/>(mt::approx<sp/>(compute_float<sp/>(),<sp/>42.0f,<sp/>0.001f));</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>The deprecated <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx</ref> (value, epsilon)</computeroutput> form, available only with <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-config_1ga67c701de5426ac340584ed038494a873" kindref="member">MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_DEPRECATED_ENABLED</ref></computeroutput>, is a value wrapper instead, which applies its tolerance to the six comparisons and to the operators; it accepts only floating-point values.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
