        <briefdescription>
<para>Generic equality comparator. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The C strings (<computeroutput>char</computeroutput> arrays, including the string literals, and <computeroutput>char</computeroutput> pointers) are compared by content, also with <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput>; a null <computeroutput>char</computeroutput> pointer is equal only to another null pointer. The other arrays (e.g. byte buffers) are compared element by element, also with a container, and written as ranges; the other pointers are compared by address. The pointers and arrays of <computeroutput>char8_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char16_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char32_t</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>wchar_t</computeroutput> are not treated as strings: the arrays are compared element by element, including the terminating null character, and the pointers by address. The integers of different signedness are compared by value, as by <computeroutput>std::cmp_equal()</computeroutput>, not after the usual arithmetic conversions, so <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gada610d1d5701b79f3df916f6e397ea06" kindref="member">eq</ref> (-1, static_cast&lt;unsigned&gt; (-1))</computeroutput> fails.</para>
<para>Both operands must satisfy <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1printable" kindref="compound">extension::printable</ref></computeroutput>, since they are reported on failure; an application type needs an <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput> for <computeroutput>mt::expression_formatter</computeroutput>, otherwise the call is rejected, with a diagnostic that names the operand type. The operands must also be comparable with the operator of the comparator, otherwise the call is rejected in the same way.</para>
<para>The same rules apply to <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gaa77076edd474fc10d8c0bd6da623e284" kindref="member">ne()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gaf32fd09749f18635233613fa48f91b56" kindref="member">gt()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1ga989e5966794d5c5487477aa782d844b1" kindref="member">ge()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gaea39573e23de35872ace5b08d2514327" kindref="member">lt()</ref></computeroutput>, and <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gaf9e47a6e18771f969cdd840ec187734a" kindref="member">le()</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the left hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the right hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Left hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Right hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A comparator object that evaluates to true if the operands are equal.</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gada610d1d5701b79f3df916f6e397ea06" kindref="member">eq</ref></computeroutput> function template provides a generic equality comparator for any types. The operands are first passed to <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a51e86043001b197561806d5c6297041b" kindref="member">detail::as_operand()</ref></computeroutput>, which converts the C strings to <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1c__string" kindref="compound">detail::c_string</ref></computeroutput>, and the other arrays to <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1array__operand" kindref="compound">detail::array_operand</ref></computeroutput>, so that they are compared by content. It constructs a comparator object, with the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1equal__to" kindref="compound">detail::equal_to</ref></computeroutput> tag, which evaluates to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if the two values are equal, and which is reported with both values if not.</para>
<para>The operands are forwarded, so that the comparator moves the temporaries and refers to the named operands, without copying them. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
